# Licensing

The plugin source (`cpp/`, `python/`, `samples/`, under `plugins/openmm/` in the
source tree), and the source tree's `Dockerfile` and `run_docker`, are released
under Apache 2.0, with component-specific licensing described below. See
[LICENSE-apache.txt](LICENSE-apache.txt) for the full text.

The components in this distribution use the following licenses:

| Component | Path | License |
|---|---|---|
| cupo runtime and API headers | `include/cupo/` and `build/libcupo.so*` in the source and runtime tarballs; `nv_openmm_plugin/lib/libcupo.so.<ABI>` in the wheel and release-channel conda packages | NVIDIA Software License Agreement (proprietary), see [LICENSE-cupo.txt](LICENSE-cupo.txt) |
| LTO-IR math objects and headers | `build/ltoir/{standard,fast_math}/cupo_math.cu.o` and `include/cupo/math/` in the source and runtime tarballs | NVIDIA Software License Agreement (proprietary), see [LICENSE-cupo.txt](LICENSE-cupo.txt) |
| Runtime CMake packages | `build/cmake/CupoRuntime/` and `share/cmake/CupoConvolution/` in the runtime tarball | NVIDIA Software License Agreement (proprietary), see [LICENSE-cupo.txt](LICENSE-cupo.txt) |
| LTO-IR examples and guides | `samples/common.sh`, `samples/ltoir-usage/` (including `usage.cu` and the reference generator), `docs/ltoir.md` and `docs/ltoir-usage.md` at the source tree's root | Apache 2.0, see [LICENSE-apache.txt](LICENSE-apache.txt) |
| LJ tail helper | `plugins/openmm/cpp/openmmapi/src/lj_tail.hpp` | Apache 2.0, see [LICENSE-apache.txt](LICENSE-apache.txt) |
| fltflt.hpp | `plugins/openmm/cpp/platforms/cuda/src/integrator/fltflt.hpp` in the source tree | BSD-3-Clause |

The third-party software in this distribution is listed, with its copyright and
license, in [NOTICE](NOTICE). THIRD-PARTY.txt has the same text. The plugin links
dynamically to OpenMM, whose CUDA platform is under the GNU Lesser General Public License; OpenMM is not
included and is installed separately.

The source distribution and GitHub tree carry identical copies of this overview,
[LICENSE-apache.txt](LICENSE-apache.txt), [LICENSE-cupo.txt](LICENSE-cupo.txt),
[NOTICE](NOTICE), and [THIRD-PARTY.txt](THIRD-PARTY.txt) at the repository root and
under `plugins/openmm/`, so the plugin directory can also be packaged on its own.
The wheel and conda packages also include these files.

### What the packages bundle, and what they retrieve

The wheel and the release-channel conda package **bundle** the cuPotential runtime
(`nv_openmm_plugin/lib/libcupo.so.<ABI>`), under the NVIDIA Software License Agreement in
[LICENSE-cupo.txt](LICENSE-cupo.txt). It is part of the distribution, not an
external material. The conda-forge plugin instead depends on the separate
`libcupo` package, which installs the runtime under the environment's `lib/`.

Separately, the install and build steps retrieve materials that are not
distributed with this software: when you build from a clone of the repository,
`run_build` and the LTO-IR sample's `run` call `fetch_cupo`, which automatically
downloads the proprietary cuPotential runtime from the GitHub release, and the installation environment
fetches separately licensed dependencies, such as OpenMM, the CUDA libraries and
Python packages, from their own sources. The tests and the `solvated_systems`
sample read OpenMM's two benchmark systems, `apoa1.pdb` and
`5dfr_solv-cube_equil.pdb`, from your OpenMM installation, or download them from
OpenMM's GitHub repository when they are absent; these files are not distributed
with cuPotential. The notice below covers those retrieved materials only.

